    overview: "The Prophet taught people that God loves noble character. Ghazali gives Ali's saying about hurrying to it, and the story of Hatim al-Ta'i's daughter among the captives. Then comes the long list of what Islam is wrapped in, and the counsel the Prophet gave Mu'adh ibn Jabal.",
    thesis: "Noble character is loved by God even in someone who was not a believer, and only those of good character will enter the Garden. The Prophet left no good counsel unsaid, and no fault without a warning.",
